1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
MEACompass: Reliability-Aware Early Prediction of Neural Network Development
from Microelectrode-Array Assays

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Toward Functional Digital Twins for Neural Organ-on-Chip Screening

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:01:00,000
By DIV7, can we forecast the DIV12 outcome for an unseen chemical—
and continue the assay when uncertainty is too high?

4
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Across five preregistered endpoints, MEACompass reduced MAE by 14.2 to 39.0
percent versus BT+, with every paired chemical-level 95 percent confidence
interval excluding zero.
Evaluation is chemical-disjoint. All doses, wells, replicates, and aliases
of a chemical remain on one side of each split.

5
00:01:40,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The registered negative control stopped the pipeline. A bounded integrity audit
found no future-derived feature or alignment defect; the failure stays visible.

6
00:02:20,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Nominal 90% intervals attained 91.0% to 92.4% coverage.
At 70% retained coverage, abstention passed on three of five endpoints.

7
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:40,000
DIV7 forecasts are available five days before the DIV12 endpoint
for accepted cases.

8
00:03:40,000 --> 00:04:15,000
DIV7 physiology is the dominant contribution family.
Chemistry adds complementary context, but not for every endpoint.

9
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:45,000
This is rat cortical neural MEA data, not organ-on-chip data.
Human neural organ-on-chip transfer requires prospective external validation.

10
00:04:45,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Forecast when evidence is strong; continue the assay when it is not.
Research decision support—not autonomous assay termination.
